 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "Fragments of a youth, far relieved now\nFrom his former burdens, and pacified,\nAs though with joy he smote those happy hands,\nAnd felt the heart that felt the world again.\nI care not if you be blind - indeed I\nOf this other sight no less ashamed;\nAnd yet my eye should see it when again\nMy spirit can manifest its delight.\nYou mean to say nothing? You are afraid?\nAre you born in vice? You say what anyone,\nA sort of love-swollen commonman, say?\nTo begin at least another question:",
